### TimeTrack API — run these from Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code (REST Client extension).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080/api/v1

### 1. Login as consultant (copy the accessToken into @token below)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "consultant@timetrack.dev",
  "password": "Demo123!"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. Who am I
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Search projects (the Angular search box calls this)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects?search=azure&page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. My time entries
GET {{baseUrl}}/time-entries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Weekly dashboard
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/weekly-summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Business rule: more than 8 hours in one entry -> 400 / 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/time-entries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "projectId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "workDate": "2026-11-09",
  "hours": 9,
  "description": "Too many hours"
}

### 7. Login as manager
# @name managerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manager@timetrack.dev",
  "password": "Demo123!"
}

###
@managerToken = {{managerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8. Pending approvals (manager only; a consultant token gets 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/approvals/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### 9. Health check (anonymous)
GET http://localhost:5080/health
